# "Sacrifice a creature" is a cost, and only your own creatures can be paid: with Bot2's Ornithopter the only creature, the
# attempted sacrifice ability rolls back. Bot1 casts its own Ornithopter - summoning sick, which a sacrifice cost does not
# mind - and the same ability then succeeds: {B}{B}. On turn five the Tower taps for {C} alone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Phyrexian Tower
Ornithopter
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Phyrexian Tower.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Tower.Activate(Ability: Sacrifice)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Tower.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
? Bot1.Mana =
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
? Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Tower.Activate(Ability: Sacrifice)
Bot1.Choose(Tap Phyrexian Tower)
Bot1.Choose(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
? Bot1.Mana = {B}{B}
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Tower.Activate(Ability: {C})
? Bot1.Mana = {C}

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
